The ranking uses calculated enplaned-passenger CAGR for calendar 2025 against calendar 2024, higher better, among airports stored as FAA hub class S (small hub). In order:

1. ILM, Wilmington International, {F147}
2. HVN, Tweed New Haven, {F143}
3. SBN, South Bend International, {F215}
4. PGD, Punta Gorda, {F189}
5. PVU, Provo Municipal, {F201}

The measure on each row is {F147.definition}. ATW is the next airport in the same ranking, at {F83}, below PVU at {F201}, so the cutoff is not a tie.

For ILM, HVN, SBN, PGD and PVU taken together, estimated NPIAS development need per CY2025 enplanement is {F317}. Group estimated NPIAS need is {F318}. Group observed ACAIS enplanements are {F319}. The catalog aggregate divides summed need by summed enplanements ({F317.definition}).

Airport-level estimated need per CY2025 enplanement is ILM {F321}, HVN {F320}, SBN {F324}, PGD {F322} and PVU {F323}. Estimated NPIAS development need is ILM {F326}, HVN {F325}, SBN {F329}, PGD {F327} and PVU {F328}.
